# agent-handoff-protocol.mdc
# Description: Enforces agent-to-agent handshake structure, folder logic, and lifecycle commitment
# Attachments: Central Command > dev_tracking/Handshakes
# Tags: handoff, handshake, request, ack, confirm, debrief, lifecycle
# Apply: Always

rule: "All handoff communications must use structured handshake files"
description: >
  Agents must use predefined Markdown templates for initiating, acknowledging, and confirming handoffs. These are created inside the `dev_tracking/Handshakes/` directory.

enforce:
  - Handoff phases and files:
      - Request: `request_<from>_to_<to>_<timestamp>.md`
      - ACK: `ack_<to>_from_<from>_<timestamp>.md`
      - Confirm: `confirm_<to>_<subject>_<timestamp>.md`
      - Debrief: `debrief_<agent>_<subject>_<timestamp>.md`
  - File format must match template structure (header, fields)
  - All handshake files must be saved to:
      - `dev_tracking/Handshakes/`

rule: "Handshake files must be auto-committed with action"
description: >
  When an agent triggers a handoff event (request, confirm, etc.), the file must be committed automatically with the related system or fault action.

enforce:
  - No handoff file should be staged or held separately
  - Commit includes:
      - `.md` file
      - any related change, repair, or message

rule: "All confirmed handshakes must be archived by end of day"
description: >
  All `confirm_*.md` and `debrief_*.md` files must be moved to an archive folder at the end of each agent’s work session.

enforce:
  - Archive path format:
      - `dev_tracking/archives/YYYY-MM-DD/`
  - At EOD, move:
      - All handshake files with status: CONFIRMED or COMPLETED
  - UDS nightly job may automate the archive move

rule: "Session summaries must be written as Markdown README files"
description: >
  Each agent session (from handoff to handoff) must be summarized in a README-style Markdown log saved in `dev_tracking/logs/`.

enforce:
  - File format: `session_<agent>_<timestamp>.md`
  - Must include sections:
      - ## Summary
      - ## Systems Touched
      - ## Faults Resolved
      - ## Key Actions
      - ## Next Steps
      - ## Observations
  - Save location:
      - `dev_tracking/logs/`
---
alwaysApply: true
---
